Description:
 i) NS2 Simulator-Introduction
1.	NS2 stands for Network Simulator Version
2.	It is an open-source event-driven simulator designed specifically for research in computer communication networks.
Features of NS2
1.	It is a discrete event simulator for networking
2.	It provides substantial support to simulate bunch of protocols like TCP, FTP, UDP, https and
3.	It simulates wired and wireless
4.	Uses TCL as its scripting
Network simulation is an important tool in developing, testing and evaluating network protocols. Simulation can be used without the target physical hardware, making it economical and practical for almost any scale of network topology and setup.
